        "reason-1": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "1",
            "title": "The leaking isn't something you're doing wrong",
            "body": "<p>Most anti-colic bottles work fine for the first few weeks. Then, without warning, milk starts finding its way out around the collar. You tighten it, loosen it, reseat the vent — it holds for a feed or two, then leaks again.</p><p>That's not an assembly problem. When a bottle depends on several plastic parts fitting together with precision, it only takes one part changing shape slightly for the whole seal to fail. Every trip through boiling water or a steriliser softens plastic just enough that it stops springing back to its original shape — so the \"sweet spot\" you're chasing keeps moving, feed after feed.</p>"
          }
        },
        "image-2": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
