        "reason-4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "4",
            "title": "Why Hosfu didn't just swap the chamber",
            "body": "<p>Hosfu was designed around the whole feeding path, not just the bottle body. Milk sits in high-borosilicate glass and flows through a soft, breast-shaped nipple angled at 15° for a more natural latch — the only two surfaces milk ever touches. The collar and other components are BPA-free PPSU, chosen because it holds its shape through repeated sterilising instead of gradually softening the way standard polypropylene does. Every material is lead-free tested.</p><p>Instead of a tube running through the milk, air returns through a vent built into the base — no straw to mis-seat, no tiny brush needed, no reservoir piece to lose. Fewer parts means fewer joints that can drift out of alignment over time. Hosfu also fits standard bottle warmers and comes with five nipple flow options, so it grows with your baby instead of needing to be replaced.</p>"
          }
        },
